/*
  holdings: claims about Digital Objects held at one state of the network,
  proved without showing the objects. Nothing here is specific to an app:
  `type` is whatever class the object's plugin gave it. App-specific claims
  (a Bitcraft drill's level, say) belong in their own predicates built on
  these.

  LiveObject(state_header, obj, tag) says:

  - `obj`'s commitment is in the created array of `state_header`, whose hash
    is a state root. The synchronizer only adds commitments from valid
    `TxFinalized` proofs, so a valid transaction made `obj`, under the rules
    of its class;
  - its nullifier, H(H(obj, obj.key), "txlib-nullifier-v1") as in
    txlib.podlang, is not in the nullifier set of `state_header`, by a Merkle
    proof of absence: nothing had consumed or re-keyed `obj` by then. Only a
    holder of `obj.key` can compute the nullifier;
  - `tag` is H(obj.stable_identifier, "dobj-object-tag-v1"). Every state of
    an object keeps its stable_identifier (TxInsert stamps it, TxMutate and
    Rekey keep it), so the tag stays the same when the object is re-keyed or
    changed, and a claim can count each object once. The string is the
    tag's domain; live.rs's TAG_VERSION is the same.

  Holds(state_header, type, tag) adds that `type` is `obj`'s class, the hash
  of its plugin's `Is<Class>` predicate, and keeps `obj` and its nullifier
  private: a verifier learns the class and the tag, and no one can watch for
  the object being spent.

  A claim is about one state: an object live there can be spent afterwards.
  A verifier checks that the state root is the network's and decides how old
  a root it accepts.

  bounty.podlang imports this module by its hash, so BountyClaim's hash pins
  it: a change here is a new version of every claim built on it.

  StateHeader matches txlib's (txlib.podlang, `record StateHeader`).
*/

record StateHeader = (block_number, block_timestamp, block_hash, created, nullifiers, prior_state_history)

// pod2 allows 5 statements per predicate; this uses all 5.
LiveObject(state_header StateHeader, obj, tag, private: index, key_hash, nullifier) = AND(
  ArrayContains(state_header.created, index, obj)
  Hash(obj, obj.key, key_hash)
  Hash(key_hash, "txlib-nullifier-v1", nullifier)
  SetNotContains(state_header.nullifiers, nullifier)
  Hash(obj.stable_identifier, "dobj-object-tag-v1", tag)
)

Holds(state_header StateHeader, type, tag, private: obj) = AND(
  LiveObject(state_header, obj, tag)
  DictContains(obj, "type", type)
)
